  "lyrics": [
    {
      "start": 0.05,
      "end": 2.902,
      "text": "Schema design is not interior decorating.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 2.902,
      "end": 7.402,
      "text": "It is a short list of goals you protect when someone asks for a new column.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 7.402,
      "end": 9.5,
      "text": "The first goal is identity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 9.5,
      "end": 14.277,
      "text": "Every row should name one thing, and you should be able to find that thing again.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 14.277,
      "end": 17.138,
      "text": "A primary key is how you keep that promise.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 17.138,
      "end": 20.333,
      "text": "The second goal is one fact in one place.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 20.333,
      "end": 21.944,
      "text": "Maya lives in Austin.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 21.944,
      "end": 27.472,
      "text": "If Austin is stored on every order, a move to Denver becomes a scavenger hunt.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 27.472,
      "end": 29.597,
      "text": "Store the city on the customer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 29.597,
      "end": 31.736,
      "text": "Let orders point at the customer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 31.736,
      "end": 33.944,
      "text": "The third goal is completeness.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 33.944,
      "end": 38.847,
      "text": "If a fact must exist, the schema should refuse a row that lacks it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 38.847,
      "end": 41.319,
      "text": "NOT NULL is a completeness tool.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 41.319,
      "end": 45.097,
      "text": "A foreign key is a completeness tool for relationships.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 45.097,
      "end": 48.055,
      "text": "The fourth goal is honesty under change.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 48.055,
      "end": 50.944,
      "text": "Updates should not create contradictions.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 50.944,
      "end": 54.291,
      "text": "Deletes should not leave orphans unless you chose that.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 54.291,
      "end": 58.388,
      "text": "The fifth goal is a schema people can query without folklore.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 58.388,
      "end": 64.027,
      "text": "If you need a five-page memo to know which total is the real total, the design is leaking.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 64.027,
      "end": 65.722,
      "text": "Speed is a later goal.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 65.722,
      "end": 71.194,
      "text": "Indexes, copies, and caches come after the facts are in the right tables.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 71.194,
      "end": 74.833,
      "text": "If you chase speed first, you freeze a messy shape.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 74.833,
      "end": 79.208,
      "text": "When a new column appears in a meeting, ask which goal it serves.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 79.208,
      "end": 84.027,
      "text": "If it serves none, it is probably a copy of a fact you already store.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 84.027,
      "end": 85.458,
      "text": "Copies want an owner.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 85.458,
      "end": 90.861,
      "text": "Either the original table, or a later denormalization you admit in public.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 90.861,
      "end": 92.847,
      "text": "Protect identity first.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 92.847,
      "end": 94.486,
      "text": "Then fight repetition.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 94.486,
      "end": 97.25,
      "text": "Then require the facts that must exist.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 97.25,
      "end": 98.944,
      "text": "Then worry about speed.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 98.944,
      "end": 102.013,
      "text": "Normalization is a method for the second goal.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 102.013,
      "end": 103.43,
      "text": "It is not a religion.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 103.43,
      "end": 107.263,
      "text": "It is a way to notice when one table is doing three jobs.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 107.263,
      "end": 111.263,
      "text": "A design that meets the goals can still be ugly on a whiteboard.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 111.263,
      "end": 114.819,
      "text": "Ugly and honest beats pretty and contradictory.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 114.819,
      "end": 117.152,
      "text": "Write the goals at the top of the sketch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 117.152,
      "end": 118.166,
      "text": "Identity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 118.166,
      "end": 119.958,
      "text": "One fact, one place.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 119.958,
      "end": 122.041,
      "text": "Required facts required.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 122.041,
      "end": 124.0,
      "text": "Change without contradiction.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 124.0,
      "end": 125.958,
      "text": "Queryable without folklore.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 125.958,
      "end": 127.152,
      "text": "Speed last.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 127.152,
      "end": 130.25,
      "text": "Then every new column has to pass the list.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 130.25,
      "end": 132.375,
      "text": "Conflicting goals will appear.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 132.375,
      "end": 137.43,
      "text": "Legal retention may force you to keep a fact you would rather normalize away.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 137.43,
      "end": 138.819,
      "text": "Write the conflict.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 138.819,
      "end": 141.152,
      "text": "Do not hide it in a mystery column.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 141.152,
      "end": 149.958,
      "text": "Audit columns \u2014 created_at, created_by \u2014 serve completeness of history, not identity of the customer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 149.958,
      "end": 154.194,
      "text": "They still belong, as long as they do not duplicate the customer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 154.194,
      "end": 159.694,
      "text": "Soft-delete flags serve honesty under change when a hard delete would smash history.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 159.694,
      "end": 163.083,
      "text": "They also complicate every query with a filter.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 163.083,
      "end": 165.958,
      "text": "That is a real trade, not a free goal.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 165.958,
      "end": 169.93,
      "text": "International addresses will test one-fact-one-place.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 169.93,
      "end": 172.666,
      "text": "A city name is not unique on Earth.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 172.666,
      "end": 176.222,
      "text": "You may need a place table sooner than the first sketch thought.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 176.222,
      "end": 178.93,
      "text": "That is the goal working, not failing.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 178.93,
      "end": 182.666,
      "text": "When product wants a dashboard tomorrow, speed shouts.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 182.666,
      "end": 185.777,
      "text": "Give them a query on honest tables first.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 185.777,
      "end": 189.819,
      "text": "If it is too slow, measure, then copy with an owner.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 189.819,
      "end": 192.666,
      "text": "The goal list is the agenda of that meeting.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 192.666,
      "end": 195.597,
      "text": "Without it, the dashboard becomes the schema.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 195.597,
      "end": 198.166,
      "text": "Teach the list to whoever can add a column.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 198.166,
      "end": 203.5,
      "text": "A schema that only the original author understands has already missed the folklore goal.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 203.5,
      "end": 210.694,
      "text": "Identity, one place, required facts, honest change, queryable shape, speed last.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 210.694,
      "end": 212.402,
      "text": "Say it until it is boring.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 212.402,
      "end": 214.666,
      "text": "Boring goals survive launches.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 214.666,
      "end": 217.18,
      "text": "A goal you cannot test is a slogan.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 217.18,
      "end": 220.791,
      "text": "Identity is tested by finding the same row tomorrow.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 220.791,
      "end": 224.555,
      "text": "One fact in one place is tested by changing it once.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 224.555,
      "end": 229.986,
      "text": "Required facts are tested by inserting a hole and watching the engine refuse.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 229.986,
      "end": 235.583,
      "text": "Honest change is tested by a delete that does not orphan, or that orphans on purpose.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 235.583,
      "end": 240.736,
      "text": "Queryable shape is tested by a new teammate writing a SELECT without a huddle.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 240.736,
      "end": 244.458,
      "text": "Speed is tested with EXPLAIN after the rest is true.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 244.458,
      "end": 247.083,
      "text": "Hang that test list next to the sketch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 247.083,
      "end": 250.972,
      "text": "Then a column request has somewhere to land besides yes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 250.972,
      "end": 254.708,
      "text": "A database that is fast and wrong is still wrong.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 254.708,
      "end": 256.916,
      "text": "The five goals are not slogans.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 256.916,
      "end": 259.444,
      "text": "They are tests you can fail on a Tuesday.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 259.444,
      "end": 264.152,
      "text": "Consistency means two tables do not disagree about the same fact.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 264.152,
      "end": 270.097,
      "text": "Integrity means the fact was allowed by the types, keys, and constraints you declared.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 270.097,
      "end": 274.861,
      "text": "Together they say: one meaning, stored once, checked at the door.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 274.97,
      "end": 285.517,
      "text": "If product price lives on products and also on every order line as a copy you never freeze on purpose, the confirmation page and the receipt can disagree.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 285.517,
      "end": 288.489,
      "text": "That disagreement is not a rounding bug.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 288.489,
      "end": 290.67,
      "text": "It is two sources of truth.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 290.67,
      "end": 298.183,
      "text": "Related entities belong in related tables, sharing a key, not sharing a pile of overlapping columns.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 298.183,
      "end": 302.267,
      "text": "Redundancy is extra copies of a fact that can drift.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 302.267,
      "end": 307.878,
      "text": "Insert, update, and delete anomalies are what drift feels like in practice.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 307.878,
      "end": 312.267,
      "text": "You change a name in one row and the old name survives in another.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 312.267,
      "end": 315.961,
      "text": "You cannot insert a fact until you invent a fake parent.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 315.961,
      "end": 321.67,
      "text": "You delete the last child and accidentally lose the only copy of a parent attribute.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 321.67,
      "end": 325.42,
      "text": "Normalization is one way to hunt those anomalies.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 325.42,
      "end": 326.947,
      "text": "Constraints are another.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 326.947,
      "end": 330.85,
      "text": "The second goal is maintainability and ease of use.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 330.85,
      "end": 336.308,
      "text": "A schema a new teammate can query without a huddle is easier to keep alive.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 336.308,
      "end": 344.114,
      "text": "Stable naming is part of that: snake_case, table names as plurals or singulars, but not both.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 344.114,
      "end": 352.517,
      "text": "customer_id everywhere, not custId in one table and customer_code in the next for the same meaning.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 352.517,
      "end": 356.225,
      "text": "The third goal is performance when the facts are already true.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 356.225,
      "end": 361.267,
      "text": "Indexes, types that fit, and joins on keys are how you buy speed.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 361.267,
      "end": 366.503,
      "text": "Speed as a first goal produces wide tables that cannot be updated safely.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 366.503,
      "end": 370.197,
      "text": "Earn integrity first, then measure the slow query.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 370.197,
      "end": 376.628,
      "text": "The fourth goal is security: who may read, who may write, what is stored in the clear.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 376.628,
      "end": 381.933,
      "text": "Access control and hashing belong here as design, not as a later patch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 381.933,
      "end": 390.267,
      "text": "The fifth goal is the ability to grow: a new attribute should not require rewriting history of unrelated tables.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 390.267,
      "end": 398.072,
      "text": "If adding email requires copying customers into a new god table, the design was a snapshot, not a schema.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 398.072,
      "end": 400.392,
      "text": "Hang the tests next to the sketch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 400.392,
      "end": 403.447,
      "text": "Identity: can I find the same row tomorrow?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 403.447,
      "end": 405.906,
      "text": "One fact: can I change it once?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 405.906,
      "end": 409.406,
      "text": "Required facts: does INSERT refuse a hole?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 409.406,
      "end": 412.628,
      "text": "Honest change: does DELETE do what I said?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 412.628,
      "end": 416.35,
      "text": "Queryable shape: can a new person write the SELECT?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 416.35,
      "end": 419.489,
      "text": "A goal you cannot test is a poster on the wall.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 419.489,
      "end": 422.433,
      "text": "Miss one goal and the app still ships.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 422.433,
      "end": 430.85,
      "text": "The regret arrives as a receipt that does not match, or a name that changes mid-trip, or a query nobody dares to touch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 430.85,
      "end": 435.322,
      "text": "Design for the five, then optimize the one that is actually slow.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 435.322,
      "end": 443.656,
      "text": "Five goals against the store: consistency so product price and receipt match unless you froze a sold price on purpose.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 443.656,
      "end": 450.197,
      "text": "Maintainability so a new analyst can find orders.customer_id without folklore.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 450.197,
      "end": 454.586,
      "text": "Performance so the home page has indexes after the keys are right.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 454.586,
      "end": 457.378,
      "text": "Security so clerks are not admins.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 457.378,
      "end": 462.892,
      "text": "Growth so a new gift-card entity is a table, not a column dump on users.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 462.892,
      "end": 466.183,
      "text": "Fail one and you will meet it as a support ticket.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 466.183,
      "end": 475.517,
      "text": "Test them in the order you can: integrity first, then naming, then EXPLAIN, then GRANT, then ALTER for the new entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 475.517,
      "end": 479.878,
      "text": "That order is how the five stay a design method, not a slide title.",
      "slide": ""
    }
  ]
}
